# CODEOWNERS -- the path boundary for this project.
#
# spec/CONTRIBUTOR_ACCESS.md layer 2. Replace {{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}} with the
# maintainer's GitHub username (keep the @), and turn on branch protection
# for the base branch: require a pull request, require review FROM CODE
# OWNERS, and do not allow bypassing for non-administrators. Without that
# protection this file is documentation, not a boundary.
#
# HOW TO READ IT. Everything not listed here is content, and content is any
# contributor's to write and merge. What is listed is what a contributor
# should not change alone: the machinery the project runs on. A pull request
# touching one of these waits for the maintainer's review.
#
# NOT hand-generated from approvers.json. That generator
# (tools/build_codeowners.py) writes the CODEOWNERS of a PRACTICE SET, where
# the owned thing is the practice text and the owners are its approvers. This
# is a document project: different question, different file, written by hand.

# /.github/ IS THE ONE THAT CANNOT BE LEFT OUT. A workflow file is executable
# code holding a token, so anyone who can edit one can rewrite every other
# protection here -- including this file, which lives under it.
/.github/          @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# Session configuration and hooks: the harness executes these.
/.claude/          @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# The vendored Precedent engine and catalogue.
/tools/            @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}
/precedent/        @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# Practice text, wherever this install materializes it.
/practices/        @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}
/local/            @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# Declares the sources in force, the visibility and the base branch.
/precedent.json    @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# The instructions every session loads.
/AGENTS.md         @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}
/CLAUDE.md         @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}

# Generated views -- a hand edit here is an edit to a generated file.
/MAP.md            @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}
/GLOSSARY.md       @{{MAINTAINER_GITHUB}}
